# Round XXIX Track A Wave 2: POSITIVE-CONTROL CANARY. `for x in Set[int]:`
# must STAY GREEN after the ggdef elaborate-layer `Ty::Set` reject on
# `Expr::Index` (see `spec/ggdef/src/elaborate/mod.rs::ast::Expr::Index`).
#
# Reason this canary exists: `spec/ggdef/src/elaborate/mod.rs::desugar_for`
# synthesizes an `Expr::Index(coll_local, idx_local)` for `for x in someSet:`,
# so an incorrect eval-layer reject would break this case (Core #15(e) Q4 —
# rule subject is USER `[]`, not any elaborated `Expr::Index`). Elaborate is
# the right layer because it sees the AST distinction; eval sees only
# `Proj::Index` after desugar and cannot tell them apart.
#
# A future contributor tempted to move the reject from elaborate to eval will
# RED this fixture — the intended failure mode.
int main():
    Set[int] s = Set[int]()
    s.add(1)
    s.add(2)
    s.add(3)
    int total = 0
    for x in s:
        total = total + x
    print(total)
    return 0
